      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A behavioral method is described in which increasing intensities of electric shocks were applied to the gasserian ganglia of alert monkeys. The animals were trained to press a lever to regulate the shock level. \"Pain thresholds\" were thereby obtained, and these thresholds were modified by varying the shock duration and by administration of morphine."},
